{
  "_about": "Plan-stage briefs for Vesper (evals/vesper_plans.py). Each brief is one composer turn: the messages, the composer's Image | Video switch, what is attached (a flat PNG per `images` label), the numbered results the thread already holds, and `expect`, which the rubric reads. The brain only ever proposes; nothing here renders, draws or charges. See docs/tasks/task-vesper-v2.md. `covers` names the coverage group a brief is in (the 30 added 2026-10-22 for the stretch widen it: clear make-now asks, long single takes, reference-heavy scenes, free looks by alias, talking photos, product pages, a project with and without a brand kit, asks to refuse or question, phone-typed, non-English, Explore); a brief may carry `project`, `explore`, `brand_kit` and `autonomy`, handed to the turn as the route hands them.",
